# nanopb options for sparkplug_b.proto
#
# These options pin fixed sizes for repeated fields so we avoid heap allocations
# at encode time. The IIoT gateway publishes a bounded, well-known set of metrics
# per NBIRTH/DBIRTH/DDATA, so static sizing is appropriate.
#
# Field paths in this file must be the fully-qualified proto path
# (org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.metrics, NOT Payload.metrics). nanopb
# compares against the parsed descriptor names.
#
# Aliases (per issue #11 design §3.5):
#   0        reserved by spec
#   1..9     sensor_type_t (TEMPERATURE..TURBIDITY) — single Double each
#   10       CUSTOM  — up to 4 Doubles (one per slot in PROTOCOL_MAX_VALUES)
#   11..13   diagnostics (UptimeMs, BatteryPercent, RssiLast)
#   total: 4 + 4 = 8 fixed metrics per DBIRTH max
#
# We allocate 16 metrics headroom for future aliases without touching the wire.
#
# Syntax: <Message>.<field> <option>:<value>
# See https://jpa.kapsi.fi/nanopb/docs/reference.html#proto-file-options

# Default string size for every string field.
*.* max_size:64

# Specific bounds per repeated field.
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.metrics                max_count:16 type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.Template.metrics       max_count:16 type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.Template.parameters    max_count:8  type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.DataSet.columns        max_count:8  type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.DataSet.types          max_count:8  type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.DataSet.rows           max_count:8  type:FT_STATIC
org.eclipse.tahu.protobuf.Payload.DataSet.Row.elements   max_count:8  type:FT_STATIC
# Note: Payload.PropertySet stays as pb_callback_t because of a circular
# dependency between PropertyValue/PropertySet (nanopb emits a warning
# otherwise). The IIoT gateway does not use PropertySet on the hot path;
# only DBIRTH *may* include a small set, and a one-shot callback there is
# acceptable (heap usage is bounded to one-shot BIRTH messages).